   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend chapter 576 of the laws of 1977 incorporating the Putnam Lake\nVolunteer Firemen's Benevolent Association and providing for its powers and\nduties, in relation to the purposes of the Putnam Lake Volunteer Firemen's\nBenevolent Association; and to repeal certain provisions of such law relating\nthereto",
    "basePrintNo": "S6364",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S6364-2023",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Rpld & add §3, Chap 576 of 1977",
    "lawSection": "Volunteer and Exempt Firefighters' Benevolent Assoc., Inc.",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S6364\n\nSPONSOR: HARCKHAM\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend chapter 576 of the laws of 1977 incorporating the Putnam\nLake Volunteer Firemen's Benevolent Association and providing for its\npowers and duties, in relation to the purposes of the Putnam Lake Volun-\nteer Firemen's Benevolent Association; and to repeal certain provisions\nof such law relating thereto\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nExpands the purposes of the Putnam Lake Volunteer Firemen's Benevolent\nAssociation; repealer\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 amends section 3 of chapter 576 of the laws of 1977 to repeal\nthe section relating to the powers and duties of the Putnam Lake Volun-\nteer Firemen's Benevolent Association and create a new section expanding\nits powers and duties.\n\nSection 2 states the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nNew York's volunteer fire departments are struggling to recruit and\nretain members at an alarming rate. Under current law, the Putnam Lake\nVolunteer Firemen's Benevolent Association is unable to provide for its\nmembers beyond what is allowed by its charter, which has a very narrow\ninterpretation of the Association's purpose. In order to allow the\nPutnam Lake Volunteer Firemen's Benevolent Association to maintain a\ncapable and enthusiastic volunteer force, its charter must be expanded.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nThis is a new bill.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATION:\n\nTo be determined.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
